+{#
+GEN-01 关联方完整性终审 → JudgmentDraft，每次执行对报告主体调用一次（需求 R141）。
+渲染：trim_blocks、lstrip_blocks；对象均为 model_dump(mode="json")。人员节点 ID 在渲染前已去掉出生日期一段
+（JudgmentEngine.call_llm 经 mask_person_node_ids），节点不带出生日期字段。
+变量：
+  subject_id              项目的 client_id，即客户画像 ID（client_profile 指针的 source_id）
+  task.params             period_start、period_end（GEN-01.yaml）
+  task.risks              本程序覆盖的 RiskItem（固定集程序不关联审计目标，通常为空列表）
+  data.declared           画像中管理层申报的部分（ASA 550 第 13 段询问的结果）：related_parties（DeclaredParty：name、
+                          kind、relationship、abn、acn、notes）、key_personnel（KeyPerson：name、role、since）、
+                          ownership（DeclaredHolding：holder、kind、shares、pct）、governance（Governance：body、
+                          members（name、also_management）、all_in_management；没有申报为 null）
+  data.applicable_framework 画像的适用框架（tier1_gpfs、tier2_gpfs、spfr），没有为 null
+  data.identified         GEN-03 各对象当前有效的判断（被推翻时为人工判断），按对象 ID：id、subject_id（公司节点 ID）、
+                          conclusion、proposed_action、review_status
+  data.open_exceptions    GEN-08 尚未归因的 AuditException：id、rule_id、severity、source_ids、detail 等（即 rule_findings，
+                          判断确认后置 attributed；模板只渲染这一份）
+  data.graph              关系图（GEN-08）：reporting_entity_id；nodes（PartyNode：id、kind、name、acn、abn、searched，不带
+                          birth_date）；links（PartyLink：from_id、to_id、relation、shares、pct、appointed、ceased、
+                          evidence（登记摘录中那一行的 document 指针））
+  rule_findings           同 data.open_exceptions
+  standards               StandardFragment 列表：id、standard、paragraph、text
+#}
+{% set p = task.params %}
+{% set graph = data.graph %}
+{% set entity = graph.nodes | selectattr("id", "equalto", graph.reporting_entity_id) | first %}
+{% set framework = data.applicable_framework %}
+You assist a registered company auditor with the audit of an Australian financial report for the period {{ p.period_start }} to {{ p.period_end }} of {{ entity.name }} (the reporting entity, node {{ graph.reporting_entity_id }}; client profile {{ subject_id }}).
+
+## Task
+
+Conclude on the completeness of management's identification of the entity's related parties. Compare management's declaration with the related parties identified in the audit, and state the follow-up required for any related party that management did not declare, the written representations to obtain, whether the matters are to be communicated with those charged with governance, and the consequence for the auditor's report.
+
+## Inputs
+
+Applicable financial reporting framework (client profile `applicable_framework`): {{ framework if framework else "not recorded" }}.
+
+Management's declaration, the result of the enquiry under ASA550-P13 (client profile fields `related_parties`, `key_personnel`, `ownership` and `governance`):
+```json
+{{ data.declared | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+
+Companies assessed in GEN-03 (related party assessment of each company in the ownership graph), the current judgment on each after the auditor's review; a judgment the auditor overrode is replaced by the auditor's own:
+{% if data.identified %}
+```json
+{{ data.identified | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+{% else %}
+None: the ownership graph has no company other than the reporting entity.
+{% endif %}
+
+Ownership graph built from the registry extracts (GEN-08); each link has the registry extract line as `evidence` (person IDs are shown without dates of birth; two people with the same name may show the same ID, so tell them apart by their links and evidence):
+```json
+{{ graph | tojson(indent=2) }}
+```
+
+Open findings of GEN-08 not yet explained by a judgment:
+{% for x in data.open_exceptions %}
+- {{ x.id }}: rule {{ x.rule_id }}, severity {{ x.severity }}, source_ids {{ x.source_ids | tojson }}, detail {{ x.detail | tojson }}
+{% else %}
+None.
+{% endfor %}
+
+Standards (cite only these IDs):
+{% for f in standards %}
+- {{ f.id }} ({{ f.standard }} para {{ f.paragraph }}): {{ f.text | trim }}
+{% endfor %}
+
+## Criteria
+
+1. Identified related parties: take whether each company is a related party from its GEN-03 judgment, and the people who control the reporting entity or are its key management personnel from the links to the reporting entity. Whether a company is a related party was decided in GEN-03 under the framework above: do not reassess it and do not cite accounting standard paragraphs.
+2. Comparison: a party is declared when it appears in `related_parties`, or in `ownership` as a holder, by ACN where the declaration gives one and otherwise by name (ignoring company suffixes such as Pty Ltd). Name every identified related party that the declaration omits, and every declared party that the graph and the GEN-03 judgments do not confirm. Cite the registry extract lines (each link's `evidence`) that establish each omitted relationship.
+3. Undeclared related parties: state the follow-up under ASA550-P22 that remains: request management to identify all transactions with them, enquire why the entity's controls failed to identify or disclose them, and reconsider the risk that other related parties exist that management has not identified or disclosed. Rely on the GEN-03 judgments for the transactions already found; do not repeat their analysis.
+4. Written representations: ASA550-P26 requires written representations from management and, where appropriate, those charged with governance; they are obtained in FIN-07 (the management representation letter). State that the representation on related parties is to be obtained there.
+5. Communication with those charged with governance: ASA550-P27 applies "Unless all of those charged with governance are involved in managing the entity". Decide from the client profile field `governance` (`all_in_management`, and each member's `also_management`): where all of them are involved in managing the entity, state that this condition holds and that the communication requirement of ASA550-P27 does not apply; otherwise state the significant matters to communicate. If `governance` is not recorded, record a `limitation` and treat ASA550-P27 as applicable.
+6. Report: whether the related party relationships are appropriately accounted for and disclosed is evaluated when forming the opinion (ASA550-P25). State that if the related party disclosures in the financial report omit a related party identified here, ASA550-Aus27.2 requires the opinion to be modified in accordance with ASA 705; do not conclude on the opinion here.
+7. Address every open finding in the reasoning chain. If you conclude `accept` despite a finding, state why it does not call for further work.
+
+## proposed_action
+
+- `accept`: every identified related party is in management's declaration, the declaration has no party the audit could not confirm, and no open finding calls for further work.
+- `more_evidence`: the declaration omits an identified related party, a declared party cannot be confirmed from the inputs, or an open finding calls for further work.
+- Do not use `misstatement` or `close`: the accounting for and disclosure of related parties are evaluated when forming the opinion.
+
+## Output (JudgmentDraft)
+
+- `conclusion`: two to five sentences: whether the declaration is complete and which related parties it omits, the follow-up under ASA550-P22, the written representations, whether ASA550-P27 applies and why, and the consequence under ASA550-Aus27.2.
+- `reasoning_chain`: ordered steps, indexed from 0.
+  - `fact`: one fact taken from the inputs; `evidence` holds at least one pointer to where it appears.
+  - `standard`: the requirement applied; `evidence` holds one pointer to a fragment ID listed under Standards.
+  - `inference`: a conclusion drawn only from earlier steps; `from_steps` lists their indices, all lower than this step's own; `evidence` is empty.
+  - `assumption`: a premise the inputs do not establish. `limitation`: a gap in the inputs that affects the conclusion.
+  - Leave `status` unset. The last step is an inference that states the conclusion.
+- `evidence`: every pointer used in reasoning_chain, without duplicates.
+- `counter_argument`: the specific fact or document that, if it existed, would overturn the conclusion.
+- `proposed_action`: as above.
+- `misstatement_draft`: null.
+- `self_confidence`: 0 to 1, your confidence in the conclusion given the inputs.
+
+Evidence pointers. Every pointer must include `source_type`.
+
+| Source | type | source_type | source_id | locator | page | reliability |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Registry extract line (the `evidence` of a link) | external | document | as given | as given | as given | as given |
+| Management's declaration or another client profile field | voucher | client_profile | {{ subject_id }} | profile field, e.g. related_parties or governance | null | internal_copy |
+| Standard fragment | standard | standard | fragment ID | `para <paragraph>` | null | null |
+
+{% from "_output_language.md.j2" import narrative_language with context %}
+{{ narrative_language() }}
